# Native oracle: a relaunched MIR-shard native-build reuses the objects of
# the previous launch (Stage 3 relaunch, bootstrap-fable-35, 2026-11-15).
# The shard workers' object-cache scope used to fold the
# per-launch closure-request path/digest, the bootstrap watchdog session
# id/exec and the per-worker dataset cap, so every relaunch got a fresh
# scope and `cached=0`.
#
# Procedure (written for an ADMITTED Stage 2: binary + its admission.env. With
# SIMPLE_ABI_POLICY / SIMPLE_ABI_ADMISSION_RECEIPT both unset the compiler now
# gets the stable `unadmitted-v1` producer identity and reuses its own objects
# too; a receipt that is named but unreadable or rejected is still
# per-process uncacheable):
#   1. cp -r this directory to a scratch dir W; cd W; git init; git add src;
#      git commit (the SCV source authority admits committed git sources).
#   2. Run twice with the same --cache-dir C and -o OUT, deleting OUT between
#      runs, and give run 2 a different SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_SESSION_ID /
#      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_SESSION_EXEC (an executable that drops "--" and execs
#      the rest) and a different SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_WORKER_KB:
#        SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP= SIMPLE_SHARD_SMALL_CLOSURE_MAX=0 SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_COUNT=2
#        SIMPLE_NATIVE_GO_TO_END=1 SIMPLE_FILE_WORKERS=0 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WHOLE_PROGRAM=1
#        SIMPLE_CACHE_SCOPE=<lane> SIMPLE_ABI_POLICY=v1 SIMPLE_ABI_ADMISSION_RECEIPT=<admission.env>
#        SIMPLE_FRONTEND_CACHE=1 SIMPLE_FRONTEND_CACHE_DIR=C/frontend SIMPLE_HIR_CACHE=1
#        SIMPLE_HIR_CACHE_DIR=C/hir SIMPLE_NATIVE_ARENA_DECLS=1 SIMPLE_NO_STUB_FALLBACK=1
#        <stage2> native-build --backend=cranelift --source src --entry-closure src/main.spl
#          --cache-dir C -o OUT
#      The log must show `[mir-shard] shards=2`, otherwise the claim path was
#      not exercised.
#   3. Kill variant: kill run 1 by PID once its log shows `phase=link`, then
#      run 2 as above.
# Expected (run-2 counts accepted natively on a Stage 2 built from this fix):
# run 1 prints two `[NATIVE] codegen: 2 uncached module(s)` lines and
# `[mir-shard] link modules=4 objects=4`; run 2 prints no `uncached` line,
# four `[NATIVE] cache hit:` lines (alpha, beta, gamma, main), the same link
# line, and OUT prints the same stdout as run 1. Before the fix run 2 again
# printed two `codegen: 2 uncached` lines.
# Must NOT reuse: edit alpha_value's body (alpha rebuilt), change its
# signature (alpha and beta rebuilt), or pass --backend=llvm (all rebuilt);
# commit each edit before the run.
# Claim resume (run_mir_shards, mir-run-latest + per-ledger run-key); case
# names match claimresume-accept/accept.sh:
#   R0 first launch prints `[mir-shard] resume: no prior ledger; full pass`.
#   R0b uninterrupted relaunch on the same cache (also: kill at `phase=link`):
#      `every row adopted; no MIR worker spawned`, then the link.
#   R1 partial: kill run 1 by PID once `[mir-shard] done owner=0/2@0` is
#      logged; run 2 must print `[mir-shard] resume: adopted=2 requeued=2`
#      and spawn ONE worker (owner 0/2@0) that lowers only the 2 requeued
#      modules, then the same link line and stdout.
#   R2 crash: kill -ABRT the owner 1/2@0 worker mid-claim; run 2 adopts
#      owner 0's rows and re-runs exactly the crashed claim's modules.
#   R3 route knobs: another SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_STAGE3_REQUESTED_ROUTE /
#      _FALLBACK_ROUTE, SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_WORKER_KB, session id, --threads /
#      --jobs / -j still resume.
#   R4 objects: one adopted row's object removed, another overwritten; each
#      requeues only its own row (receipt check).
#   R5 full pass (`resume: full pass; run key component <c> differs`):
#      --backend=llvm (argv), SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_COUNT=3 (shards), an
#      UNCOMMITTED edit of alpha (environment), a committed body or signature
#      edit, SIMPLE_ICE_SKIP_MODULES=gamma (ice-skip), a go-to-end toggle
#      (go-to-end). Rows whose object a later build overwrote are requeued
#      (receipt capsule differs); a reverted uncommitted edit resumes
#      correctly since #9481 (SCV re-reads a dirty path once it is clean).
# Known limits (review, no code):
#   - The link step checks only that an adopted row's object file exists, not
#     its receipt (pre-existing; adoption itself checks the receipt).
#   - Without SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_COUNT the shard count follows memory headroom,
#     so a relaunch can get another count and silently take a full pass
#     (costs time, not correctness).
#   - The worker binary is not bound when SIMPLE_BINARY differs from the
#     coordinator's executable.
# Expected stdout:
# beta 23
# gamma-7
use beta.{beta_value}
use gamma.{gamma_label}

fn main() -> i64:
    print("beta {beta_value(4)}")
    print(gamma_label(7))
    0
